{
  "id": "06843_haideru",
  "headword": "{這|は}い{出|で}る",
  "reading": "はいでる",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to crawl out",
  "conjugation": {
    "type": "ichidan",
    "stem": "{這|は}い{出|で}"
  },
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to crawl out, to creep out",
      "explanation": "To emerge by crawling; to come out on hands and knees or by dragging oneself."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "06843_haideru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{虫|むし}が{穴|あな}から{這|は}い{出|で}てきた。",
      "english": "An insect crawled out of the hole.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06843_haideru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{赤|あか}ちゃんがベッドから{這|は}い{出|で}た。",
      "english": "The baby crawled out of the bed.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06843_haideru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{瓦礫|がれき}の{下|した}から{這|は}い{出|で}ることができた。",
      "english": "I was able to crawl out from under the rubble.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "06843_haideru_ex4",
      "japanese": "{布団|ふとん}から{這|は}い{出|で}る{気力|きりょく}がない。",
      "english": "I don't have the energy to crawl out of the futon.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "{這|は}い{出|で}る is a compound verb: {這|は}う (to crawl) + {出|で}る (to come out).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: Intransitive ({自動詞|じどうし})\n- Pattern: Xから{這|は}い{出|で}る\n- Transitive pair: {這|は}い{出|だ}す (to cause to crawl out)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n- {這|は}い{出|で}ている - is in the process of crawling out\n- Telic: describes the action with a clear endpoint (emerging)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {穴|あな}から{這|は}い{出|で}る - to crawl out of a hole\n- {布団|ふとん}から{這|は}い{出|で}る - to drag oneself out of bed\n- やっと{這|は}い{出|で}る - to finally crawl out\n\nCOMPOUND VERB NOTES:\nThe ～{出|で}る pattern indicates movement outward. Combined with {這|は}う, it describes emerging by crawling motion.",
